Round 3 (2026-02-26)

What changed this round
- Files changed: `clang/aot/_.c`.
- `aot_force_dup` was upgraded from single-step to bounded multi-step DP forcing:
  - new limit: `#define AOT_FORCE_DUP_FUEL 32`;
  - loop continues while the current term is `DP0/DP1` and fuel remains;
  - each step uses the same conservative DUP dispatch set as before (`NAM/BJV/BJ0/BJ1`, `LAM`, `SUP`, `DRY/MAT/SWI/USE/INC`, `ERA/ANY/PRI/NUM`, `C00..C16`);
  - no full `wnf()` call is used.
- Fixed a high-severity `heap_take` restore bug:
  - SUB fast-path now restores the taken cell with `heap_set_rel(loc, cell)` before returning/continuing with payload;
  - unknown-payload fallback now also restores with `heap_set_rel` (was relaxed `heap_set`).

Why this shape
- Multi-thread safety: `heap_take` does atomic exchange to 0 when `THREAD_COUNT > 1`; any early return without restore can leave a permanent zero hole/spin risk.
- Performance boundary: bounded DUP-only forcing resolves common DP chains without the pathological over-evaluation seen when calling full `wnf`.
- Semantic boundary remains conservative:
  - if forcing reaches non-DP, return it;
  - if payload is unknown/non-dispatchable, restore and return current DP unchanged;
  - if fuel exhausts, return current term as-is.

